    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "",
      "transparent": true,
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 31,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 3
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**How it works:** the board measures (stable weight, spikes removed, signed). At the on-call % the system **warns** (*pickup_needed*) — it does not book. A **person presses Book truck**. When the truck arrives, the system tells the board over MQTT; the board **detects the emptying itself**. Every lift is then **judged** (≥60% / <60% / Full 2h+) and its **CO₂** counted. Some trucks are late and the old fixed route sometimes comes early — on purpose, so you see every case."
      },
      "id": 113
    }
